<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kutir-Nahhunte</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kutir-Nahhunte was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shutrukid-dynasty">Shutrukid dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a>, the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shutruk-nahhunte">Shutruk-Nahhunte</a>. Around 1158 BCE father and son defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassite-dynasty">Kassite dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, carrying off monuments such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victory-stele-of-naram-sin">Victory Stele of Naram-Sin</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/code-of-hammurabi">Code of Hammurabi</a> to Susa. This period marked the military zenith of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a>.</p></div>
